<title>GERMANY: German crops prosper in damp and cool weather.</title>
<headline>German crops prosper in damp and cool weather.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rainfall in May has brought relief to dry German soils and cold temperatures are not bad enough to hamper crop growth, the DWD meteorological office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Grain and beet crops are developing very well,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>&quot;Moisture levels are now ideal with the exception perhaps of northern Bavaria and some eastern German regions.&quot;</p>
<p>Winter rapeseed continued to bloom in the north and looked in good shape elsewhere.</p>
<p>Forecasts for the next seven days are for changeable weather with maximum day temperatures of 15-20 degrees, DWD's weekly report said.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
